WEBVTT

00:00.984 --> 00:02.984
The new term starts today.

00:03.320 --> 00:06.632
And I'll be in a new class
on my third year.

00:07.032 --> 00:10.410
Well, I have to know which class I'm in...

00:10.744 --> 00:13.330
Hey, Icchi! You're in the same class!

00:13.330 --> 00:14.181
What?

00:14.540 --> 00:16.125
With me.

00:17.417 --> 00:19.670
Aren't you happy about it?

00:19.670 --> 00:20.337
(Congratulations for passing)
(Class Change)

00:20.337 --> 00:23.048
I've been avoiding
thinking about the class change.

00:23.632 --> 00:27.094
(3-1, Kyotaro Ichikawa)
I mean, if I'm split up with Yamada...

00:27.553 --> 00:30.139
...it's a small world, after all, so.

00:32.223 --> 00:35.519
(To Kyo) (I only checked my own name)
(I'm in my new class right now)

01:05.632 --> 01:06.717
Kyotaro!

01:12.739 --> 01:15.158
I said be mindful of your distance!

01:24.651 --> 01:26.778
Ah, sorry! Wrong person!

01:27.529 --> 01:28.880
I'm with you, Rin!

01:28.880 --> 01:29.631
What?!

01:30.324 --> 01:32.993
No, no, no, no! This can't be happening!

03:04.543 --> 03:07.020
Be mindful of your distance
when in front of other people.

03:07.587 --> 03:09.506
This is our task for
this new academic year.

03:09.715 --> 03:10.924
But...

03:11.275 --> 03:15.771
We're not dating, so having to
not get too close is a bit weird...

03:15.771 --> 03:17.139
We're in the same class again!

03:17.639 --> 03:21.910
Aw, geez! Anna, you always get
way too close with everyone you meet!

03:21.910 --> 03:22.686
Right, right!

03:22.911 --> 03:25.439
Like, you always get all touchy with them!

03:25.439 --> 03:26.790
Thank you for cleaning up after our mess!

03:26.790 --> 03:28.650
Even with boys! Look.

03:32.946 --> 03:34.131
What?

03:34.131 --> 03:35.157
Nothin'.

03:35.741 --> 03:36.992
Oh! Na!

03:37.909 --> 03:39.369
- Huh?
- Hm?

03:40.662 --> 03:42.748
I'm... actually...

03:46.626 --> 03:48.420
...in your class too!

03:48.770 --> 03:52.566
Y-Yeah, our names are right next to
each other, so I already know that.

03:52.716 --> 03:54.926
Your last names are
Yamada and Yoshida, so...

03:56.770 --> 03:59.865
- Alright! - Alright!
- So embarrassing!

04:00.198 --> 04:01.909
Ah! Chi!

04:02.601 --> 04:05.495
I think I flunked.

04:06.730 --> 04:10.734
Her name wasn't in class 3-1's list,
and reality came crashing down...

04:10.734 --> 04:11.568
No!

04:13.695 --> 04:15.172
I wasn't on any of them!

04:15.447 --> 04:19.159
So does that mean you somehow
transferred schools without knowing?

04:19.159 --> 04:20.010
Huh?!

04:20.243 --> 04:21.803
Nothing we can do, then.

04:21.803 --> 04:23.914
- Nothing we can do.
- Don't do that!

04:23.914 --> 04:25.015
(Faculty Room)

04:25.015 --> 04:26.416
Kobayashi?

04:26.666 --> 04:29.394
Um... wait, let me see.

04:29.836 --> 04:31.438
Oh, there it is.

04:32.672 --> 04:35.775
Drum roll please... and bam!

04:36.176 --> 04:37.319
You're in 3-1.

04:38.345 --> 04:39.721
That's great!

04:39.721 --> 04:40.989
The teacher made a mistake.

04:40.989 --> 04:42.324
Let's get to class.

04:43.975 --> 04:46.728
T-This must've been done on purpose!

04:46.728 --> 04:49.981
- Chi, wear your slippers first.
- That's true, right?! Right?!

04:49.981 --> 04:51.983
I'm sure that's how it is!

04:53.749 --> 04:55.487
Oh! What's wrong, Ichikawa?

04:56.905 --> 04:58.240
Something of concern?

04:58.448 --> 05:00.367
N-No, nothing in particular.

05:00.909 --> 05:03.203
I was just worried she'll be too anxious.

05:06.832 --> 05:07.833
See, boss?

05:08.250 --> 05:10.669
I told you he's completely fine.

05:10.961 --> 05:12.170
Now, then.

05:12.437 --> 05:14.523
So this is our new classroom!

05:14.673 --> 05:17.092
Aren't you happy we did all that?

05:17.092 --> 05:18.902
- We're back!
- Welcome back.

05:18.902 --> 05:21.363
Oh! Ruu and Yuka, you're here!

05:21.363 --> 05:22.740
Fellow basketball girls, huh?

05:23.473 --> 05:24.516
Moepi!

05:24.933 --> 05:26.143
Oh, Kan-Kan!

05:26.351 --> 05:28.119
We're in the same class again!

05:28.119 --> 05:29.871
Yurine's here, too!

05:29.871 --> 05:31.273
We went to karaoke, didn't we?

05:38.405 --> 05:39.322
Moepi!

05:39.322 --> 05:40.390
Kan-Kan!

05:40.390 --> 05:42.175
- Serina!
- Kan-Kan!

05:42.175 --> 05:43.702
- Moepi!
- Kan-Kan!

05:43.702 --> 05:46.137
Sneak...

05:46.137 --> 05:47.706
Sneak sneak...

05:49.166 --> 05:52.210
- Boo! Pat pat pat...
- What are you doing?

05:56.756 --> 05:57.340
What's this?

05:57.340 --> 05:59.843
(Stay here later)

05:59.843 --> 06:01.553
(Class 3-1)

06:01.970 --> 06:04.055
I'll be your homeroom teacher
from today onwards!

06:04.489 --> 06:07.008
I'm the energetic Moriya!

06:07.008 --> 06:08.685
Well, it's fine.

06:08.977 --> 06:13.023
Let's enjoy this small world
to the fullest.

06:20.405 --> 06:21.715
RIP.

06:21.924 --> 06:25.010
I've been waiting for you here
while peeking under the girls' skirts.

06:25.010 --> 06:25.911
What is it?

06:26.203 --> 06:29.189
So how's class 3-1, Ichikawa?
Made any friends?

06:29.189 --> 06:32.392
Seen any panties? Fondled any breasts?

06:32.392 --> 06:34.628
This isn't an ecchi romcom!

06:34.628 --> 06:36.896
Argh! Must be nice being in class 3-1!

06:36.896 --> 06:39.591
Not only there is Yamada,
but there is also Hanzawa!

06:39.591 --> 06:42.819
You've even got 2-2's leader, Ando!

06:42.819 --> 06:45.071
All the top girls are in there!

06:45.071 --> 06:47.682
Are you the NPC
giving me exposition in the tutorial?

06:48.141 --> 06:52.829
Alright. I wanna hear all about 3-1
on the way back home today with 3-2's Ota.

06:52.829 --> 06:54.523
Including panties stories!

06:54.523 --> 06:55.649
Huh?

06:57.793 --> 07:00.695
- Going to club meeting?
- We're third-years now, so...

07:00.695 --> 07:03.573
Third-years, huh? Time sure flies...

07:08.995 --> 07:10.805
Tap tap tap...

07:11.373 --> 07:13.817
- Bam!
- Why did you ask me to stay?

07:13.817 --> 07:15.959
Right! About that...

07:16.628 --> 07:18.647
Here! I've been meaning to give you this.

07:18.647 --> 07:19.381
Huh?

07:20.298 --> 07:21.316
Okay...

07:27.305 --> 07:28.948
Happy birthday!

07:30.600 --> 07:31.810
No, not there!

07:32.394 --> 07:33.812
This is for your wallet.

07:36.648 --> 07:38.108
Also, like...

07:38.108 --> 07:41.595
There are three classes, but aren't like
half of ours people from 2-3?

07:41.595 --> 07:42.837
Yeah, well.

07:42.837 --> 07:46.032
I'm closer to people from 2-2, so...

07:46.592 --> 07:51.262
Also, like,
is Yamada dating that Ichikawa guy?

07:53.206 --> 07:55.041
- Who knows.
- Deny it!

07:55.292 --> 07:57.168
Is that a bad thing if it's true?

07:57.168 --> 07:59.671
It's not like Anna's forbidden to date.

07:59.671 --> 08:01.523
Of course it's not a bad thing!

08:01.523 --> 08:04.551
I wanna give them a grand celebration!

08:04.843 --> 08:07.987
(Be happy!)
There were people with mutual feelings in 2-2,

08:07.987 --> 08:11.347
and we arranged a whole flashmob
for their confession!

08:11.348 --> 08:12.851
It was a huge success!

08:12.934 --> 08:15.967
We made them sing and dance together
during our school festival play, too!

08:15.967 --> 08:17.664
It was so much fun!

08:18.481 --> 08:20.667
I wanna do that again.

08:20.667 --> 08:23.236
She's saying some hellish stuff.

08:23.570 --> 08:26.756
I heard those two broke up
over the spring break.

08:26.756 --> 08:28.133
What? Really?

08:28.133 --> 08:29.743
Not enough love in the air?

08:29.951 --> 08:31.302
No, Kan-Kan.

08:31.302 --> 08:33.163
You see, flashmobs and stuff is like...

08:34.748 --> 08:36.832
(Congrats!)

08:39.169 --> 08:40.837
They sound so fun!

08:41.837 --> 08:44.841
We prepared, like, a bunch of confetti!

08:44.841 --> 08:46.426
- And party poppers? - And party poppers!
- Hey!

08:51.765 --> 08:53.183
Are we dating?

08:53.408 --> 08:54.284
Huh?

08:55.685 --> 08:57.579
That's... what they said, right?

08:57.812 --> 08:58.938
Ah, right...

09:02.609 --> 09:04.134
Oops, I forgot someth...

09:07.364 --> 09:10.308
I'm not gonna clean up after
your mess anymore, okay?!

09:12.827 --> 09:14.304
How was it, Ichikawa?

09:14.304 --> 09:15.805
Saw any panties?

09:15.805 --> 09:17.682
No, my panties got seen.

09:17.682 --> 09:19.934
Must be nice being in 3-1!

09:19.934 --> 09:21.670
Sekine's in 3-1 too, right?

09:21.670 --> 09:24.547
Huh? I don't really care.
I don't really care, see.

09:24.964 --> 09:26.399
Ichikawa, which one do you like?

09:26.399 --> 09:29.110
Why do you think I get to choose?

09:29.110 --> 09:33.306
Come on, tell me what you think!
About your new class!

09:33.890 --> 09:35.558
It's not like I feel anything myself,

09:35.558 --> 09:38.620
but people from other classes
are envious of me, so I feel good.

09:38.853 --> 09:40.146
This one's got a bad personality.

09:40.730 --> 09:42.065
I'm in 3-1 too.

09:42.357 --> 09:43.983
Wait, you are?

09:44.401 --> 09:47.904
During lunch break,
I went to 3-2, where Hara is.

09:48.488 --> 09:50.448
They got split up, huh...

09:50.824 --> 09:55.011
I only hadn't seen her for 45 minutes,
but she already got a little prettier!

09:55.011 --> 09:56.621
Your girlfriend is from outside Tokyo?

09:57.122 --> 10:00.350
Hara being in another class is
pretty nice to see, too...

10:00.350 --> 10:01.751
Some sort of new kink?

10:04.879 --> 10:06.879
Must be nice, Ichikawa.

10:06.879 --> 10:08.675
You're in the same class as Yamada.

10:08.675 --> 10:10.093
Well, yeah...

10:10.593 --> 10:11.386
Why's that?

10:11.636 --> 10:13.196
What?! Oh, uh, nothing!

10:13.196 --> 10:15.557
I, I mean, Yamada's pretty, so.

10:15.557 --> 10:17.242
You've never thought of her that way!

10:24.357 --> 10:26.693
She's who I'm closest with, so.

10:27.277 --> 10:28.403
Ah...

10:29.279 --> 10:30.530
I see.

10:31.656 --> 10:35.702
I didn't want to do anything weird
to make him feel small.

10:36.703 --> 10:37.454
Huh?

10:37.996 --> 10:39.205
I'll be going this way.

10:39.748 --> 10:41.458
Let's go home together again sometime.

10:41.958 --> 10:45.420
Is it because
I think of Adachi as a friend?

10:45.962 --> 10:47.172
Sometime, huh...

10:51.009 --> 10:51.926
Boo!

10:53.219 --> 10:54.345
You sure are busy.

10:55.263 --> 10:57.015
The new academic year has started.

10:57.932 --> 11:00.101
(Nurse's Office)

11:03.563 --> 11:05.665
Don't do that, Kobayashi.

11:06.274 --> 11:07.525
She's not doing it!

11:09.027 --> 11:11.004
I'm making myself taller with my spirit!

11:11.004 --> 11:12.639
Oh, with your spirit?

11:12.639 --> 11:14.616
- Next, please!
- I see.

11:15.867 --> 11:17.468
I'll put in some spirit!

11:18.986 --> 11:20.830
Sucking in like that is pointless.

11:21.748 --> 11:24.584
Today is our physical check
that we do at the start of every year.

11:24.810 --> 11:27.478
Ugh, it was not good at all...

11:27.478 --> 11:29.756
(Physical Check: Kyotaro Ichikawa)
And the results are...

11:31.341 --> 11:33.067
Show me yours, too!

11:33.067 --> 11:34.010
I wasn't looking at yours!

11:37.281 --> 11:39.490
I told you to not get too close
in front of other people!

11:39.490 --> 11:41.684
You're the one who spoke up first!

11:42.435 --> 11:47.524
The celebration girl who set up
that hellish flashy confession event...

11:48.066 --> 11:51.027
She's the only one I hope doesn't find out
about my feelings for Yamada.

11:51.236 --> 11:55.281
I don't wanna be forced into
doing a flashy confession like that!

11:55.281 --> 11:56.699
Are you two...

11:58.576 --> 11:59.244
Beep?

12:00.203 --> 12:03.306
I think "beep" means our relationship
is closer than normal.

12:03.623 --> 12:04.766
Ah, no...

12:05.166 --> 12:07.877
I mean, you heard Ms. Moriya, right?

12:08.270 --> 12:12.924
April is the month to talk to people
you haven't talked much with before!

12:12.924 --> 12:16.286
Everyone, make a hundred friends, okay?

12:16.553 --> 12:18.404
So in order to get a good report, I...

12:18.721 --> 12:19.782
You know.

12:20.557 --> 12:22.100
I see.

12:23.393 --> 12:24.577
By the way,

12:24.577 --> 12:27.497
I've never talked to you either, Yamada.

12:27.497 --> 12:28.831
Oh, you're right!

12:28.831 --> 12:30.525
You can call me Kan-Kan.

12:30.525 --> 12:32.919
Hmm... can I call you Kanna?

12:32.919 --> 12:33.736
Why?!

12:34.153 --> 12:36.447
I want a special nickname for you!

12:39.659 --> 12:42.095
It's so long, but it's so pretty!

12:42.387 --> 12:44.998
Don't just let her into
your heart like that!

12:49.586 --> 12:51.337
Kanna is already my nickname for her.

12:51.562 --> 12:53.022
Oh, I'm sorry!

12:53.022 --> 12:56.301
Sorry! Yamada tends to
get close to people easily.

12:56.885 --> 13:00.430
Hanzawa, we were pretty close
back in elementary school.

13:01.389 --> 13:02.365
Been a long time.

13:03.132 --> 13:04.365
You're acting like she's your ex.

13:04.851 --> 13:07.645
Then, how about I call you Panda?

13:07.645 --> 13:09.372
What's this one based on? Scary.

13:09.480 --> 13:11.499
Then, I'll call you A. Yamada.

13:11.499 --> 13:12.667
Oh, sure!

13:12.667 --> 13:13.484
You're fine with it?

13:13.902 --> 13:15.378
- A. Yamada.
- Panda!

13:15.378 --> 13:16.921
- A. Yamada.
- Panda!

13:16.921 --> 13:18.172
- Yamada.
- Panda!

13:18.172 --> 13:19.632
I didn't say the "A" part!

13:19.632 --> 13:21.884
I'm alone as I've always been...

13:22.468 --> 13:23.970
(Library)

13:30.251 --> 13:31.169
What are you doing?

13:33.046 --> 13:36.799
I was just thinking about how
I can reach the shelf above now.

13:37.050 --> 13:38.718
You did grow taller by a lot!

13:38.902 --> 13:40.094
Six centimeters.

13:40.970 --> 13:42.180
That much in the past year.

13:44.807 --> 13:45.850
That's amazing!

13:46.559 --> 13:49.979
I grew 15 centimeters taller
when I was in fifth grade, though.

13:49.979 --> 13:52.231
Can you not say stuff like that?

13:52.440 --> 13:55.126
Well, I still have room for growth.

13:55.126 --> 13:56.627
It's like an athlete's interview!

13:58.696 --> 13:59.614
What?

14:00.448 --> 14:03.301
I wanna leave a record
of our current heights.

14:03.301 --> 14:04.953
It's recorded in data.

14:04.953 --> 14:06.679
Not something like that.

14:06.679 --> 14:07.956
- Oh, right!
- What?

14:08.222 --> 14:09.716
Back in the day,

14:09.717 --> 14:13.211
people used to leave records of
their children's heights on their house pillars!

14:13.628 --> 14:16.047
Ichikawa, stand against the pillar.

14:16.589 --> 14:19.400
Wait, don't just vandalize stuff.
That's a permanent marker.

14:20.802 --> 14:23.079
Hmm... this one's water-based!

14:23.079 --> 14:26.157
Also, if we write it somewhere apparent,
it'll get erased right away.

14:26.157 --> 14:26.849
You're right.

14:31.062 --> 14:32.605
Okay, stay there like that.

14:35.900 --> 14:37.819
Around this tall?

14:37.819 --> 14:38.879
Alright.

14:38.879 --> 14:40.797
Can't you feel
just a little guilty about it?

14:40.797 --> 14:42.090
Mark my height, too!

14:42.090 --> 14:43.741
Clear the books from the shelf above.

14:43.741 --> 14:45.718
Didn't you say you can reach it now?

14:45.718 --> 14:46.953
I'll get a chair.

14:53.601 --> 14:55.962
(Kyo)

15:01.926 --> 15:03.986
Has your voice finished changing?

15:03.986 --> 15:06.305
Huh? Um, well...

15:07.056 --> 15:08.282
Alright, done.

15:09.851 --> 15:12.270
How tall am I? Let me see!

15:12.270 --> 15:14.313
(Anna)

15:20.194 --> 15:23.156
Twirl... twirl... twirl...

15:26.367 --> 15:27.869
Before this,

15:28.411 --> 15:32.957
I actually thought,
maybe I didn't want to be an adult.

15:33.624 --> 15:37.128
But now I've realized
that I wanna get closer to you, Yamada.

15:37.754 --> 15:39.047
Physically.

15:47.472 --> 15:48.556
You can.

15:49.265 --> 15:50.700
I'm fine with it.

15:51.350 --> 15:52.268
Huh?

15:55.780 --> 15:56.981
What? Uh...

16:06.407 --> 16:08.176
I meant in height...

16:10.161 --> 16:11.496
I'm sorry!

16:11.496 --> 16:13.122
I want to tell her.

16:14.582 --> 16:15.374
Yamada.

16:16.918 --> 16:18.169
About my feelings...

16:22.215 --> 16:23.299
If I wait longer...

16:25.009 --> 16:26.636
Someone will find...

16:27.178 --> 16:28.763
...out!

16:33.535 --> 16:36.646
No response?
Not interested in romance, huh?

16:36.896 --> 16:38.896
I mean, we weren't doing anything.

16:39.065 --> 16:40.833
Was I being too self-conscious?

16:40.833 --> 16:41.609
Hey.

16:43.861 --> 16:45.630
You were about to say something.

16:45.630 --> 16:48.699
A-Ah, um...

16:50.868 --> 16:51.911
- Huh?
- Huh?

17:12.056 --> 17:13.598
That gave me a shock!

17:14.058 --> 17:15.518
Oh, something fell.

17:16.060 --> 17:17.854
(Class: Sunflower. Name: Yurine Hanzawa)

17:18.813 --> 17:20.248
A book about deep sea fishes.

17:20.248 --> 17:22.358
It has her name on it.
Seems like it's hers.

17:22.358 --> 17:24.585
(Class: Sunflower. Name: Yurine Hanzawa)
I'll give it back to her.

17:26.112 --> 17:27.320
The next day...

17:27.946 --> 17:30.825
Our first seat assignment
in our third year...

17:31.534 --> 17:34.136
I don't care where I end up sitting.

17:34.136 --> 17:36.706
More importantly, Yurine Hanzawa...

17:37.039 --> 17:40.626
She seems to be the best friend
of that threatening celebration girl.

17:41.294 --> 17:45.923
I mean, she seems like the cool type
who won't gossip about other people, so...

17:49.820 --> 17:51.345
It's the main character seat!

17:51.971 --> 17:53.440
- Yamada.
- Yeah?

17:53.441 --> 17:56.867
I have bad vision,
so do you want to switch seats with me?

17:56.867 --> 17:57.894
Sure.

17:58.227 --> 17:59.270
Alright.

18:03.900 --> 18:06.335
No, don't do stuff like this!

18:06.335 --> 18:09.614
I'm the type to push back when
something is set up for me!

18:10.448 --> 18:13.409
Pretend... pretend like
she's a stranger...

18:13.409 --> 18:16.787
No, don't! Don't smile like that!

18:21.250 --> 18:23.060
Anna Yamada, you said?

18:23.461 --> 18:26.464
Pfft. I guess you're somewhat passable.

18:29.818 --> 18:30.760
Ew!

18:30.760 --> 18:32.611
It's like the start of a shojo manga!

18:34.597 --> 18:36.390
Hey, let me see your textbook.

18:36.390 --> 18:37.950
Hmph. Not a chance.

18:39.101 --> 18:43.356
I'm letting that close distance we got
to waste like that...

18:46.025 --> 18:47.902
(Sorry)

18:48.110 --> 18:49.528
So painful...

18:53.366 --> 18:56.661
Yamada left early today,
so we didn't get to talk at all.

18:57.328 --> 18:59.705
- Bye bye!
- Minding the distance too much...

19:00.164 --> 19:02.416
What if she does
become distant after this?

19:03.292 --> 19:06.754
Yamada might get sick
of my distrust of people, too.

19:09.006 --> 19:11.801
Hanzawa's book.
She still hasn't returned it?

19:12.468 --> 19:14.220
No choice, then. I'll do it instea...

19:17.365 --> 19:20.034
(To Hanzawa)
A letter. It's Yamada's handwriting.

19:20.657 --> 19:23.479
I think you might've misunderstood,
so I'm writing this to clear things up.

19:23.980 --> 19:26.399
I'm very close with Ichikawa,

19:26.732 --> 19:28.985
but we're not dating or anything.

19:29.277 --> 19:31.362
In parentheses: As of today, April 10th.

19:31.737 --> 19:34.965
But that's not my main point.

19:34.965 --> 19:38.119
Ichikawa's really shy, you see.

19:38.452 --> 19:40.538
Sometimes it hurts me to see

19:40.871 --> 19:43.057
how much he thinks about other people.

19:43.308 --> 19:47.003
He pulls away when you get close,
like a cat, really.

19:47.461 --> 19:50.214
And bit by bit, by bit...

19:50.214 --> 19:52.591
We built that relationship, slowly.

19:53.509 --> 19:55.136
The time we spent,
and the distance between us...

19:55.594 --> 19:59.181
To me, they are special and precious.

19:59.974 --> 20:00.891
So...

20:01.642 --> 20:04.979
So, please don't worry about us.

20:05.271 --> 20:07.940
I'd be happy if you can just leave him be.

20:08.649 --> 20:10.126
Ichikawa's...

20:10.126 --> 20:11.235
I shouldn't keep reading.

20:20.911 --> 20:22.121
Morning!

20:25.082 --> 20:27.082
("I...")

20:27.710 --> 20:28.711
Morning.

20:30.338 --> 20:32.757
("...Want to Get Closer to Yamada")

20:35.468 --> 20:37.153
(Library)

20:37.153 --> 20:38.804
The close distance we've built...

20:39.680 --> 20:41.432
...is the most important thing to me.

20:41.849 --> 20:43.784
I'm sorry for doing unnecessary stuff.

20:43.784 --> 20:44.702
No, it's fine.

20:46.145 --> 20:50.358
You know, I wanna know
how love feels like...

20:50.775 --> 20:52.777
Is it different to friendship?

20:53.110 --> 20:54.737
Or admiration?

20:55.154 --> 20:58.199
It's a good thing,
but we can't celebrate it?

20:58.824 --> 21:01.202
Why did that couple last year break up?

21:02.787 --> 21:06.207
Did we... do a bad thing?

21:09.353 --> 21:10.871
I-Ichikawa!

21:11.337 --> 21:12.338
Bye, now.

21:12.814 --> 21:15.299
Hanzawa, let's exchange LINE accounts!

21:16.175 --> 21:19.845
I'll teach you all about it, okay?

21:22.364 --> 21:23.697
I-I'd rather you not!

21:23.697 --> 21:25.409
Huh? Wait, what?

21:25.684 --> 21:28.854
You should mind your distance
with everybody, no matter who.

21:28.854 --> 21:29.772
Why?!

21:29.772 --> 21:32.942
("I Want to Get Closer to Yamada")
